From: Plain Browser
Subject: [defaults] HTTPS-First Mode on by default, in its balanced setting

Category: 90-defaults. Chromium 156 ships HTTPS-First Mode's balanced setting ("Warn you before going to insecure
public sites") but leaves it off unless the user turns it on. Plain Browser turns it on for every profile whose user
has not chosen: navigations are tried over HTTPS first and a public site that only answers over HTTP gets the
"Connection is not secure" warning; local and non-unique hosts (192.168.x.x, *.local, intranet names) are not
warned about. Settings > Privacy and security > Security > "Always use secure connections" shows the setting
(GeneratedHttpsFirstModePref reads the same IsBalancedModeEnabled()), and a choice made there (off, balanced or
strict) is stored in the prefs and wins over this default.
---
--- a/chrome/common/chrome_features.cc
+++ b/chrome/common/chrome_features.cc
@@ -1230,6 +1230,7 @@
 // Automatically enables HTTPS-First Mode in a balanced configuration when
 // possible.
+// Plain Browser: on by default (patches/90-defaults/0001).
 BASE_FEATURE(kHttpsFirstBalancedModeAutoEnable,
-             base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+             base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 // Kill switch for crbug.com/40892208.
